<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mihranid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th–9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Mihranids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mihranid dynasty was a princely family of Persian origin that ruled Caucasian Albania from the early seventh century until the early ninth. Claiming descent from the Sasanian noble house of Mihran, its princes, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javanshir">Javanshir</a>, balanced between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a> and the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>. Under them the Albanian church flourished and missions were sent to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> of the north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>.</p></div>
